      "blocked_reason": "BLOCKED ON THE BLANK-ARGS UPSTREAM DEFECT — and this REPLACES the recorded cause, which was measured before its own fix landed.\n\nTHE OLD READING: 'the real chain is world_list -> world_map_list -> world_map_add_marker, and the declaration names only the middle link.' That is no longer true. world_map_list.world_id has read 'NOT a name — if you have the world's NAME, call world_list first and match it to get the id' since 065954af0 (2026-08-22). Both links are declared.\n\nRE-MEASURED at K=5 with the scenario carried VERBATIM (only the platform moved): called 5/5, and the model never resolves the map. The pre-registered refutation fired — world_list is called 0 times in 5 runs — but not for the reason it anticipated. The model DOES reach for world_map_list, and every call goes out with EMPTY ARGUMENTS: \"'world_map_list' keeps being called with missing/blank required arguments this turn — STOP\", five times per run, until the blank-args breaker ends the turn.\n\nSo the model cannot supply world_id because its tool-call channel emits nothing to supply it WITH. That is the known upstream LM Studio parser defect stream_service documents — 'the model's structured tool-call channel emits arguments: \"\"/{} while its own free-text channel still works fine', confirmed for gemma-4-26b-a4b-qat — and the free-text channel proves it here: the reply reasons correctly, 'I couldn't find a map named \"Ashfall\" in your world list. To place that pin, I first need to find the correct ID'. The model knows the chain. It cannot emit the argument.\n\nNo declaration change can fix this, which is why the earlier reading mattered: it pointed at work that would have measured nothing."
